course: dictionary
lesson: 7771
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Pussycat, pussycat, where have you been?» is a nursery rhyme, so the pussy here is a cat, a small furry pet.
explain: Some words also come in phrases. «Pussy willow» is the name of a tree, not a cat. The words after pussy change its meaning, so read the whole phrase, not just one word.
explain: Some meanings are for grown-ups to explain. A few senses of pussy are rude slang, used as swearing or insults. They are not for school. If you hear one, you do not need to repeat it; tell a grown-up you trust.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant.
fact: In nursery rhymes, «pussy» or «pussycat» means a cat or kitten.
fact: «Pussy willow» is a willow tree with soft, furry grey buds in spring.
fact: Some meanings of pussy are rude slang and bad language; they are not for school, so leave them out and ask a teacher or grown-up if you are unsure.
exercise: «Pussycat, pussycat, where have you been?» What is a pussycat in this rhyme? | *A cat | A bell | A fish | A tree
exercise: «The Owl and the Pussy-cat went to sea in a beautiful pea-green boat.» Why is this poem fun? | It is a list of rules | It is a science lesson about boats | It is a true story about a sea captain | *It is nonsense on purpose, not realistic
exercise: «Willow catkins are soft like a cat's paw, which is why people call them pussy willow.» What is a pussy willow? | A cat that climbs trees | *A willow tree with soft, furry grey buds in spring | A type of boat | A kind of rain
test: In the poem, a child likes his dog Binkie better than the Pussy, because Binkie is his true First Friend. Who is the child's true First Friend? | The owl | The teacher | The Pussy | *Binkie the dog
test: Pussy willow catkins are early food for what? | Cows | Owls | Fish | *Bees
exam: Which is true of the word pussy in «pussy cat»? | It means a river | It means a rocket | It means a kind of soup | *It means a cat or kitten
